# FRB.html

Dataset: mag-obs — Measured magnetic inclination and total field: 186 observatories (annual means)
  and 2,147 survey stations, with IGRF-14
File: data/mag/raw/obs/FRB.html
SHA-256: a30322eeb235a71857835e66e73eec0af9fb4d56a55172aa25235f6e24b5d38b (also in
  data/mag/inputs.lock; check with: cd data/mag && sha256sum -c inputs.lock)
In the public repository: no, only this description and the hash: The BGS World Data Centre allows
  scientific use with acknowledgement but does not say that its pages and answers may be
  republished; only the hash and the source are given. Get it from fog fetch mag-obs, then compare
  its SHA-256 with the one above.
Obtained: values extracted from web pages.
From: BGS WDC annual-means page of each observatory (fog fetch mag-obs).
Check it yourself: fog verify mag-obs (tools/) downloads it again into a temporary directory and
  compares it with this hash.
What could still be wrong: Values are supplied by the observatory operators; a few years are flagged
  provisional on the pages.
Collected: 2026-09-27/2026-10-14
Licence: other — BGS World Data Centre for Geomagnetism (Edinburgh): data free for scientific use
  with acknowledgement of the WDC and the observatory operators / survey institutes; IGRF-14 (IAGA)
  public.
Sources:
- BGS World Data Centre for Geomagnetism (Edinburgh), Worldwide Observatory Annual Means; values
  supplied by the observatory operators
  <https://geomag.bgs.ac.uk/data_service/data/annual_means.shtml>
- BGS World Data Centre for Geomagnetism (Edinburgh), Global Survey Data (repeat stations and
  one-off stations), via the WDC API; values supplied by national survey institutes
  <https://wdcapi.bgs.ac.uk/global-geomagnetic-survey>
- IAGA, International Geomagnetic Reference Field, 14th generation (IGRF-14) coefficients
  <https://www.ngdc.noaa.gov/IAGA/vmod/coeffs/igrf14coeffs.txt>
Evidence class (rule 10): check
Where the Earth's radius enters:
- IGRF-14 (igrf14coeffs.txt): magnetic latitude from the IGRF pole, a model fitted on the globe; the
  measured I and F themselves carry no radius
What would vindicate the flat model (rule 5): A flat residual box centred on zero and as narrow as
  the globe's, with the same median north and south of the magnetic equator; or a field-strength box
  narrower than every globe box.
